menu "gPlug-mini"

config GPLUG_SIM_METER
    bool "Simulated meter data (never ship)"
    default n
    help
        Feeds the aggregator from an embedded capture instead of the meter UART.
        Selected by building with sdkconfig.sim.defaults. A production image must
        never have this set; CI verifies that by inspecting the built binary.

comment "Network — provisional, until the captive portal writes NVS"

# The bench AP is a NetworkManager connection named gplug-bench that owns wlan0
# and autoconnects, so the workbench's own /api/wifi/ap_start cannot have the
# radio. The device joins that AP instead; these are bench credentials for a
# bench network, not secrets.
#
# BOTH benches broadcast this SSID, and both are ipv4.method=shared, so both
# gateways are 10.42.0.1. The device joins whichever is stronger and there is no
# way to tell from the device which one that was: the address it gets and the
# broker it dials are identical either way. Start the broker on both, or the
# device lands on the quiet one and reports only a TCP error.

config GPLUG_WIFI_SSID
    string "WiFi SSID"
    default "gplug-bench"
    help
        Compile-time credentials, so a bench run needs no provisioning step.
        A deployed device is provisioned through its captive portal and reads
        credentials from NVS; until that exists, these are how it joins.

config GPLUG_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "WiFi password"
    default "benchtest123"

config GPLUG_MQTT_URI
    string "MQTT broker URI"
    default "mqtt://10.42.0.1:1883"
    help
        The bench AP is a NetworkManager shared connection, so the Pi is at
        10.42.0.1 on that network and mosquitto listens on all interfaces.

endmenu
